Upstream
--------

The engine (src/sunshine_apps_ui/core) began as bazzite-sunshine-manager by
wadiebs, by way of 4o66's fork of it, and was folded into this project rather
than kept as a separate program alongside it. It is derived from

    https://github.com/wadiebs/bazzite-sunshine-manager

built on commit 4bedee5 (2026-04-19), which upstream calls version 2.0.

That work is licensed under the MIT License, and its notice is preserved
verbatim in LICENSE.upstream-MIT, exactly as upstream published it -- including
its copyright line, which names no holder. Nothing here relicenses it: upstream's
code remains available from upstream under MIT, and the MIT terms continue to
apply to it.

What is licensed under the GPL is this fork's own additions and the combined
work they form. The MIT License permits that: it allows a derivative to be
distributed under other terms provided its copyright and permission notice are
retained, which is what LICENSE.upstream-MIT is for.

One consequence, recorded so it is not rediscovered the hard way: patches from
this fork can no longer be offered to upstream, because an MIT project cannot
take GPL code without relicensing. Two pull requests were filed before this
change (wadiebs/bazzite-sunshine-manager#34 and #35); those were offered to an
MIT project and remain MIT. Anything sent upstream from here on would have to be
offered separately under MIT.
